## Ignore Visual Studio temporary files, build results, and
## files generated by popular Visual Studio add-ons.
##
## Get latest from https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/VisualStudio.gitignore

# ── npm-workspace re-inclusion (MUST precede the global artifact rules below) ──
# The TypeScript CI/CD-integrations workspace lives at /packages. The NuGet
# "packages folder" rule would otherwise ignore it, so here we (1) keep ignoring
# NuGet restore output in any packages/ folder and (2) re-include the root
# workspace. This block is placed BEFORE all the global build/secret/artifact
# rules that follow, so EVERY one of those later rules (compiler output, publishing
# profiles/scripts, BuildLog, BenchmarkDotNet, bin/obj, Debug/Release, symbols,
# NuGet, VS, logs, test results, secrets) re-applies to files under /packages —
# because a later matching rule wins. Only workspace SOURCE (never matched by any
# ignore rule) is therefore tracked. A Node/JS-ecosystem safety net for categories
# the VisualStudio rules don't cover is appended at the END of this file.
**/[Pp]ackages/*
!**/[Pp]ackages/build/
!/packages/*
!/packages/**
# Re-ignore NuGet restore output NESTED inside the workspace (e.g. a nested C#
# project's `packages/` restore dir), which the broad `!/packages/**` re-inclusion
# above would otherwise EXPOSE. The workspace ROOT `/packages` stays included; only the
# CONTENTS of a `packages/`/`Packages/` directory nested BELOW it are ignored again. We
# ignore `.../[Pp]ackages/*` (the contents) rather than the directory itself, because
# git will not descend into an IGNORED DIRECTORY, so the `build/` re-inclusion below
# could never take effect if the directory were ignored. A `**` here matches zero or
# more intermediate segments, so both `/packages/packages/` and `/packages/<proj>/packages/`
# are covered. Its own `build/` stays re-included.
/packages/**/[Pp]ackages/*
!/packages/**/[Pp]ackages/build/


